The engine's side, measured in the simulator at patches 168-272
(2026-10-13), for chrome-demo.py's flags (docs/wasm-hcaptcha-measurement.md,
"Record, replay"):

  engine-globals.txt   --globals      the window names in hCaptcha's frames
  engine-only.txt      --add-globals  those Chromium lacks, plus the three
                                      EventTarget methods the engine has as
                                      window's own
  engine-enum.txt      --enum-keys    Object.keys(window) in the challenge frame
  own-layout.json      --own-layout   own keys of navigator, document, ...
  engine-request.json  --transplant   the engine's getcaptcha request, in
                                      plain text before hsw encrypts it
  harness-names.js     prepend to hsw-record.js for VITA_SIM_INJECT: the
                       names Chromium's recording harness adds to window,
                       so both name lists match

The aligned run: --strip-gap --globals engine-globals.txt --values --mimic
--add-globals engine-only.txt --global-tag --own-layout own-layout.json
--enum-keys engine-enum.txt --record DIR
